1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,500
A coding agent made this
video with explainroo.

2
00:00:03,675 --> 00:00:05,045
It didn't use a video model,

3
00:00:05,415 --> 00:00:07,785
an API key or a video editor.

4
00:00:08,130 --> 00:00:10,780
Everything you see is
drawn with JavaScript.

5
00:00:12,410 --> 00:00:15,580
explainroo is a free,
open source kit for coding agents.

6
00:00:15,945 --> 00:00:17,535
The agent writes two files.

7
00:00:17,910 --> 00:00:20,080
The first one is the script for the voice.

8
00:00:20,425 --> 00:00:23,915
The second one is a bit of
JavaScript that draws the pictures.

9
00:00:25,083 --> 00:00:27,793
A voice model called
Kokoro reads the script.

10
00:00:28,093 --> 00:00:29,723
It runs on your own computer.

11
00:00:30,098 --> 00:00:34,348
Then Whisper listens to the recording
and writes down the time of each word.

12
00:00:35,350 --> 00:00:38,980
This way a picture can appear at
the moment the voice mentions it.

13
00:00:39,170 --> 00:00:42,780
The agent writes one line of code,
and when the voice says database,

14
00:00:43,170 --> 00:00:44,380
the database appears.

15
00:00:45,550 --> 00:00:47,820
Chrome draws each frame in the background.

16
00:00:48,145 --> 00:00:49,995
There are five looks to pick from,

17
00:00:50,265 --> 00:00:53,495
and explainroo also makes the
music and the sound effects.

18
00:00:54,550 --> 00:00:56,400
The agent can't watch the video,

19
00:00:56,770 --> 00:00:59,760
so explainroo turns it into
things the agent can read.

20
00:01:00,055 --> 00:01:04,395
It makes still pictures of each scene
and contact sheets that show a scene over

21
00:01:04,395 --> 00:01:05,005
time.

22
00:01:05,270 --> 00:01:10,480
A check also finds text that is cut off,
bad timing and words the voice got wrong.

23
00:01:11,483 --> 00:01:14,793
One command turns all
of it into an MP4 file.

24
00:01:16,983 --> 00:01:19,133
explainroo is free and open source.

25
00:01:19,493 --> 00:01:22,443
The code and these example
videos are on GitHub.

